===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|mi|makō|gloss=shark}}, a Southern Maori dialect form of the more standard {{m|mi|mangō|gloss=shark}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Either of two powerful [[mackerel shark]]s of the genus {{taxfmt|Isurus|genus}}, having a large heavy body, a sharp nose and a nearly symmetrical tail, found in southern oceans.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2022|author=[[w:Percival Everett|Percival Everett]]|title=Dr. No|publisher=Influx Press (2023)|page=101|passage=‘Aguedo fell through the floor into what we call the shark pool. We call it that because it is a pool filled with sharks. '''Mako sharks''', to be precise.’}}

